Experimental Linux RV64/LP64D context switching.

Save the psABI callee-saved integer and floating-point registers and fcsr.
Deferred callbacks run on the destination stack before it resumes; dying
threads never save or access their old stack after switching away.

Runtime validation on RV64 Linux, using an OverlayBD build configured with
test dependencies installed:
  cmake -S "$src" -B "$build" -DPHOTON_BUILD_TESTING=ON -DBUILD_TESTING=ON
  cmake --build "$build" --target test-riscv64-context
  ctest --test-dir "$build/_deps/photon-build" -R '^test-riscv64-context$' --output-on-failure
Run in both Debug and Release configurations, including a build with
-fno-omit-frame-pointer. Cross-built tests need a RISC-V machine or an
explicitly configured QEMU runner and a compatible target userspace.
This backend remains experimental until these runtime tests pass.

